# Operator standards

The authoritative rules live in `.agent/rules/operator-standards.md`, relative to the
repository root. Read that file before changing a controller, a status update, or anything
under `api/`. This stub deliberately keeps no copy of the rules.

It covers idempotent level-triggered reconciliation and requeue semantics, status updates
through the subresource with `ObservedGeneration`, finalizer naming and deletion races,
structured logging via `log.FromContext(ctx)`, watch and predicate choices, and which
generated files must never be hand-edited.

Note the codegen requirement: after changing CRD or model types under `api/` run
`make generate manifests reference`, and after changing Helm values run `make helm-reference`.
CI checks all four targets, so a dirty tree fails the PR.

